  "ai_language_tip": "Use polite standard Russian (ru); it is the everyday business language. Belarusian (be) is co-official but uncommon on service lines; reply in it only if the other side uses it. English is limited outside Minsk hotels.",
  "english_ok": "rarely — Some younger staff in Minsk hotels and central restaurants; clinics, garages, taxis and state offices are Russian only.",
  "politeness": "Formal 'Вы'; 'Здравствуйте' + on whose behalf you call; close with 'Спасибо, до свидания'. Calm, formal and to the point.",
  "name_tip": "Bookings 'на фамилию …'; gendered surnames (-ов/-ова, -ич is not gendered); spell Latin names letter by letter.",
  "phone_tip": "Mobile +375 29 / 33 / 44 / 25 then 7 digits (e.g. +375 29 12345678); domestically 8 029 12345678; Minsk landline 8 017; Viber and Telegram common for confirmations.",
  "time_tip": "24h in writing; spoken 'в половине восьмого' = 7:30, 'без пятнадцати восемь' = 7:45; read back in 24h.",
  "number_tip": "Phone numbers are read as the operator code, then a 3-2-2 group read as whole numbers (hundreds, then two pairs); read back group by group; collective numerals for people ('нас трое', 'на двоих').",
  "avoid_calling": "Avoid 13:00–14:00 lunch at clinics/offices, restaurant peaks, and calls after 21:00; Sunday for offices.",
  "closed_days": "Shops and restaurants mostly 7 days; state offices and many clinics closed Sunday, short Saturday; holidays 1–2 January, 7 January, 8 March, Radunitsa (moves with Orthodox Easter), 1 and 9 May, 3 July, 7 November, 25 December; some are moved by government work-day transfers.",
  "booking_channels": "Relax.by for restaurant tables, takeaway and salon booking; 103.by and Talon.by for doctors (public polyclinics and private centres); Yandex Go and Yandex Eda plus local delivery apps; phone and Viber for small businesses.",
  "voice_menu": "Polyclinic registries (регистратура), mobile operators (A1, MTS, life:)), banks and Belpochta use IVR; small venues answer directly.",
  "callback_habits": "Talon.by and clinics send SMS reminders; restaurants may call back to confirm large bookings; small businesses confirm in Viber.",
